<Base
  title="Leigh Scholten: About"
  description="Designer in Melbourne, Lead UX Designer at RACV."
>
  <article class="detail">
    <header class="detail__header" data-reveal>
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="detail__body" data-reveal-children>
      <p>
        I'm a designer in Melbourne and Lead UX Designer on RACV's app team. Before
        RACV I built a small team to design Western Union's multicurrency digital
        wallet for Australia, inside a global design system that has to flex.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before that I spent six years at ANZ. I was one of the principal designers on
        ANZ Plus, from the first concept to a digital bank used by millions of
        Australians. I led the design system across iOS, Android, web, email and AEM.
        Its components get more than five times the use of their ANZ Classic
        equivalents.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most of my work has been in financial services. What I care about is the
        systems and design infrastructure that let product teams move quickly without
        breaking things for customers. I've mentored designers for more than ten years. Five
        of the people I worked with at ANZ moved into senior or leadership roles
        while I was there.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside the day job I run <a href="https://leroice.com">leroice</a>, my
        creative practice. It covers design system tooling, brand work and the odd 3D
        illustration project. It's where I practise the things product work doesn't
        always ask for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
